  "goodToKnow": "Der Oldtimer is a pseudo-English word for a vintage or classic vehicle, not an old person. In Germany, cars over 30 years old in good original condition can get an H-Kennzeichen (historic number plate) with lower tax and exemption from city low-emission zones. The VW Käfer (Beetle), built in Wolfsburg from 1945 and in Mexico until 2003, and the Mercedes 300 SL are classics. Plural: die Oldtimer."
